# Settings for Privilege demo LAB. Mock mode needs none of them.
#
# The app reads ONE settings file, ~/Development/.env (mode 600), or the file STANDALONE_ENV names. Real environment variables win.
# Only the keys below are read from it. Never put admin or worker credentials in it: they belong in ~/.config/demo-kit/provisioning.json
# and this app never reads that file. The app ignores (and names) any such key it finds.
# This file is only a list of the keys: copy the lines you need into ~/Development/.env, with real values.

# mock (default: everything in process, nothing leaves the machine) or live. The Mock/Live toggle in the header changes it at run time.
# In the shared file the key is PRIVILEGE_DEMO_MODE; as an environment variable it is DEMO_MODE.
# PRIVILEGE_DEMO_MODE=mock

# Vertical pack: generic (default, the original demo) or utility (utility / NERC CIP-style, invented groups, mock backends).
# PACK=generic

# --- Live mode only (owner-run): Bearer access tokens from your PingFederate are verified against its JWKS ---
# Base URL of your PingFederate. https (http only for loopback, or hosts named in PF_HTTP_HOSTS).
# PF_URL=https://pingfederate.example
# The audience your PingFederate puts in access tokens for this app.
# PF_AUDIENCE=privilege-demo
# Optional: PF_ISSUER (defaults to PF_URL), PF_JWKS_URL (defaults to PF_URL/pf/JWKS), CLOCK_SKEW_SEC (default 30, capped at 60).

# --- Optional ---
# DATA_DIR=.data            policies and audit log live here (one folder per workspace under workspaces/)
# APPROVAL_TTL_MS=600000    how long a held call waits for an approver
# SESSION_SECRET=           signs the persona cookie; unset means sessions end when the app restarts
